# Results and Discussion

Comparison of Phase Transition Properties of HELPs. Following the same molecular biology strategy used to obtain the HELP synthetic gene,23 a second gene named HELP1 was produced in our lab.24 A schematic drawing of the primary structures of the recombinantly expressed biopolymers is presented in Figure 1. In both cases, one monomer (based on a naturally occurring human elastin sequence) was chosen as the basic unit to be reiterated. The backbone of both polypeptides consisted of eight peptide units corresponding to the most regularly repeated domain of human elastin coded by exon 24. HELP1 (calculated molecular weight, \(37205\;\mathrm{Da}\)), is characterized by a more continuous, repetitive structure as compared to HELP. In the HELP macromolecule (calculated molecular weight, \(44886\,\mathrm{Da}\)), the peptide sequence is rich in alanine-lysine cross-linking domains interspersed among the hydrophobic regions. The presence of \(\upalpha\)-helical tracts is expected in the HELP biopolymer, which is well-documented for the elastin crosslinking domains.32,33

The hydrophobic and hydrophilic tendencies of the polypeptide chains (hydropathy index) were evaluated according to Kyte and Doolittle.29 All of the artificial peptides \((\mathrm{VPGVG})_{100}\) and \((\mathrm{VAPGVG})_{90}\), which mimic the hydrophobic domains of mammalian elastin and the recombinant HELPs yielded similar values for the calculated mean hydropathy index (GRAVY). However, a different percentage of the sum of polar and charged amino acids was observed for HELP \((5.1\%)\) and HELP1 \((0.6\%)\), the hydropathy index did not change significantly, showing a difference of less than \(1\%\) (Table 1). HELPs biopolymers without the histidine-tag sequence were also evaluated showing that, even in presence of marked changes in pI, the GRAVY index resulted only slightly affected, with variations less than \(7\%\). As reported by other authors for elastin-like polypeptides above \(30\ \mathrm{KDa}\) based on the VPGVG motif, the presence of a six histidine-tag sequence lead only to a slight reduction in Tt.10

